  ('24ac2e0e-3a35-4f94-a701-831127b96883','Buckskin Bowmen is a club based in Waterloo, New York, a small Seneca County village in the heart of the Finger Lakes region. As a club rather than a commercial operation, it likely runs on a schedule its members set themselves, with a range they maintain collectively rather than a business open to the general public on posted hours. No information on course type, target count, or program offerings is included in this listing, so it functions best as a starting point for further inquiry rather than a full picture of what''s on offer. Anyone in the Finger Lakes area interested in archery or club membership should reach out to Buckskin Bowmen directly to confirm current access and activities.'),
  ('7e8b2916-4006-4ec6-8767-91693a69c366','There''s a Buckskin Bowmen Archery Club in Gwinn, Michigan, a small community in the Upper Peninsula''s Marquette County, an area known for dense forest and a deeply rooted hunting tradition. As a volunteer club, it''s likely run and maintained by its own members rather than operating with posted public hours, which is typical for archery ranges in this part of the U.P. No details on course layout, target types, or how to visit are included in this listing. Given the Upper Peninsula''s remote character, reaching the club directly, whether by phone or through local hunting circles, is probably the most reliable way to confirm current activity, access, and membership details before making the trip out.'),
  ('3453e388-4ea1-4761-8830-8b614be158df','Buffalo Field Archery Club in Houston stands out for combining three things at once: an actual 3D course, a field course, and lessons, all under one volunteer-run club. That''s a rare mix in a metro as large as Houston, where most archery options lean either purely commercial or purely informal. The field course setup, shooting at varied and often uphill or downhill angles over a marked trail, is a different discipline from 3D animal targets, and having both on the same grounds gives members a genuinely broad range of practice. Lessons being available also opens the club to newcomers rather than just experienced bowhunters. Specific schedules and how to enroll in lessons aren''t listed here, so contact the club directly for current details.'),
  ('7639b351-a1ef-42b2-b791-daa972a32ce2','Buffalo Ridge Archery operates as a commercial archery business in Goodlettsville, Tennessee, a Nashville suburb along the Cumberland River known for its family-friendly growth in recent years. As a commercial operation, it''s likely set up for walk-in customers rather than requiring club membership, though this listing doesn''t specify whether it offers an indoor range, a pro shop, lessons, or any combination of those. Middle Tennessee has a growing archery scene as the Nashville metro expands, and businesses like this tend to fill in as new suburbs need local options. Anyone in the Goodlettsville area curious about visiting, whether for range time or equipment, should contact Buffalo Ridge Archery directly to confirm current hours and services offered.'),
  ('c1bd5abb-4b51-4eff-beb4-a476c0574a9f','Build A Bowtique, judging by the name, is a commercial archery business in Tampa, Florida likely focused on custom bow building and equipment rather than operating primarily as a shooting range. Tampa''s archery market serves a mix of bowhunters preparing for Florida''s long hunting seasons and target shooters looking for gear and setup work. This listing doesn''t confirm whether the business has an in-house range, offers lessons, or is purely retail and service focused, so those specifics shouldn''t be assumed either way. Anyone in the Tampa Bay area looking to have a bow built, tuned, or fitted should contact Build A Bowtique directly to ask about current services, since a name like this usually points to specialized work rather than a general storefront.'),
  ('fa6d5718-5f1e-4dff-86c8-a4f6f42650b4','Bullock''s Archery is a commercial archery business located in Ventura, California, on the Central Coast where the archery community tends to be smaller and more spread out than in the Los Angeles basin to the south. As a commercial operation, it likely serves both target shooters and bowhunters preparing for California''s deer and hog seasons, though this listing doesn''t confirm whether it includes an indoor or outdoor range, a pro shop, or lessons. Ventura County''s coastal and mountain terrain both support hunting, so a local archery business here fills a real gap for equipment and service. Anyone in the area interested in visiting should contact Bullock''s Archery directly to confirm current hours and what services are actually offered on site.'),
  ('46918a34-a346-4a5b-8bf2-ac385af587d1','Bullseye Jim''s Archery is a commercial archery shop in East Greenbush, New York, just across the Hudson from Albany, offering both a pro shop and lessons under one roof. That pairing means new archers in the Capital Region can get instruction and buy or tune equipment without needing to visit separate businesses, while experienced shooters have a local option for tuning ahead of hunting season. Named after its owner, the shop has the feel of a personal, hands-on operation rather than a big-box retailer. Lane counts, specific lesson formats, and pricing aren''t part of this listing, so anyone interested should contact Bullseye Jim''s Archery directly to ask about current offerings and scheduling.')
